\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s10 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Description\
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 The NSRunLoop class declares the programmatic interface to objects that manage input sources. An NSRunLoop processes input for sources such as mouse and keyboard events from the window system, NSPorts, NSTimers, POSIX file descriptors, and NSConnections.\
\fs14\
\fs28 In general, your application won\'27t need to either create or explicitly manage NSRunLoop objects. Each thread has an NSRunLoop object automatically created for it. The NSApplication object creates a default thread and therefore creates a default run loop.\
\fs14\
\fs28 If you do want to perform your own explicit run loop management, you do so by running the current thread\'27s run loop (returned by the class method \b currentRunLoop\b0 ) with an \i input mode\i0  that specifies the type of input to be received. The currently defined input modes are:\
\fs14\
\pard \s61 \li6753 \fi-4838 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9525 \fs28 NSDefaultRunLoopMode\tab Use this mode to deal with input sources other than NSConnections. Defined in the \b Foundation/NSRunLoop.h\b0  header file. \
\fs14\
\fs28 NSConnectionReplyMode\tab Use this mode to indicate NSConnection objects waiting for replies. Defined in the \b Foundation/NSConnection.h\b0  header file.\
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 In addition, the Application Kit defines these modes:\
\fs14\
\pard \s61 \li6753 \fi-4838 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9525 \fs28 NSModalPanelRunLoopMode\tab Use this mode when waiting for input from a modal panel, such as NSSavePanel or NSOpenPanel. Defined in the \b AppKit/NSApplication.h\b0  header file. \
\fs14\
\fs28 NSEventTrackingRunLoopMode\tab Use this mode for event tracking loops. Defined in the \b AppKit/NSApplication.h\b0  header file\
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 Each input mode has a list of \i input sources\i0  (NSPorts, NSTimers, or NSConnections) associated with it. Each input source has a limit date associated with it. For NSPorts, the limit date is a timeout value, after which input from that port is no longer timely. For NSTimers, the limit date specifies when the timer should fire. (When a timer fires, it sends a specified message to a specified object, and it may be scheduled to fire again later. See the NSTimer class specification for more information.) \
\fs14\
\fs28 When an NSRunLoop runs, it polls each of the sources for the input mode to determine which one has the earliest limit date. During this polling, the input sources may process any input they have queued. Once the NSRunLoop determines the earliest limit date for this input mode, it solicits input from the operating system up to that limit date. If input arrives, it is processed. At that point, the NSRunLoop may either return or it may continue, depending on which method was used to run the loop. \
\fs14\
\fs28 For example:\
\fs14\
\pard \s20 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx2413 \tx2889 \tx3421 \tx3953 \tx4457 \tx4933 \tx7005 \tx7509 \tx8013 \tx8517 \tx9021 \tx9525 \tx10029 \tx10533 \tx11037 \tx11513 \f2 \fs24 NSRunLoop *theLoop = [NSRunLoop currentRunLoop];\
\
[theLoop acceptInputForMode:NSDefaultRunLoopMode beforeDate:[theLoop \
\fi0 \tab limitDateForMode:NSDefaultRunLoopMode]];\
\fs14\
\f1 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 The method \b limitDateForMode:\b0  returns the earliest limit date of all the input sources for the mode NSDefaultRunLoopMode. \b acceptInputForMode:beforeDate:\b0  runs the loop until that date, processing any input it receives until that time. As a convenience, you can use \b runMode:beforeDate:\b0  instead. It invokes \b acceptInputForMode:beforeDate:\b0  and \b limitDateForMode:\b0  with the mode you supply. \
\fs14\
\fs28 To continuously run in NSDefaultRunLoopMode, you can use either of the methods \b run\b0  or \b runUntilDate:\b0 . To run another mode continuously, invoke \b runMode:beforeDate:\b0  in a loop with a date far in the future:\
\fs14\
\pard \s20 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx2413 \tx2889 \tx3421 \tx3953 \tx4457 \tx4933 \tx7005 \tx7509 \tx8013 \tx8517 \tx9021 \tx9525 \tx10029 \tx10533 \tx11037 \tx11513 \f2 \fs24 while ([[NSRunLoop currentRunLoop] runMode:NSModalPanelRunLoopMode \
\fi0 \tab beforeDate:[NSDate distantFuture]])\
\fi0 \tab ;\
\fs70\
